    "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "Hello o/ \r\n\r\nMini.colors is excellent for making quick adjustments to current colorscheme based on environment, (e.g., such as outdoors). That said, I often find myself spending too much time trying to remember specific configurations - I almost always have to open a new split and navigate to :h MiniColors, then search for the /recipes section. \r\n\r\nIt would be neat to have these recipes right away in the interactive buffer, allowing users to make immediate adjustments by uncommenting lines. This would also allows users to save split for :hi instead of :h MiniColors.\r\n\r\nLet me know what you think!\r\n",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hello o/</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Mini.colors is excellent for making quick adjustments to current colorscheme based on environment, (e.g., such as outdoors). That said, I often find myself spending too much time trying to remember specific configurations - I almost always have to open a new split and navigate to :h MiniColors, then search for the /recipes section.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It would be neat to have these recipes right away in the interactive buffer, allowing users to make immediate adjustments by uncommenting lines. This would also allows users to save split for :hi instead of :h MiniColors.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Let me know what you think!</p>",
    "bodyText": "Hello o/\nMini.colors is excellent for making quick adjustments to current colorscheme based on environment, (e.g., such as outdoors). That said, I often find myself spending too much time trying to remember specific configurations - I almost always have to open a new split and navigate to :h MiniColors, then search for the /recipes section.\nIt would be neat to have these recipes right away in the interactive buffer, allowing users to make immediate adjustments by uncommenting lines. This would also allows users to save split for :hi instead of :h MiniColors.\nLet me know what you think!",
